Ladybird locates an inline containing block without in-flow fragments
using its absolute child’s recorded line position. Its content height
and top follow the line’s baseline and the inline’s font metrics. An
otherwise empty line contributes no height. Both pseudo-elements and
ordinary absolute children use the same containing-block rectangle.

Blink’s InlineItemsBuilderTemplate::ExitInline requests a box fragment
for empty inlines, including those with only absolute children.
WebKit’s InlineDisplayContentBuilder::processNonBidiContent obtains an
inline’s rectangle from LineBox::logicalBorderBoxForInlineBox, keeping
its position on the line. Gecko’s nsInlineFrame::ReflowFrames retains
the inline frame’s size. ComputeInlineAbsoluteCBRect derives the
containing block from the inline fragments’ padding edges, and
nsBlockFrame::ReflowAbsoluteFramesInInlineFrame uses that rectangle.
Ladybird recovers the geometry from recorded line markers without
adding an in-flow fragment that would give an empty line height.

Chrome 157 confirmed the empty and whitespace-containing inline cases
for ::before, ::after, and an ordinary absolute child. It also keeps
both the container and the inline at zero height on an empty line.
